<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span><span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> Theory</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose a re-parametrization of the generalized advantage estimation so they can be taken advantage of by critic-free methods such as GRPO.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Full Version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 Bounding the normalized advantage estimation bias ‣ 3 GRPO-𝜆 for rapid reward propagation ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we take a look at GRPO’s advantage estimation, which is centered around producing multiple rollouts from the start-state <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using their resulting scores to estimate <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mean return of all states <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{s^{0}_{t},\dots,s^{g-1}_{t}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{s^{0}_{t},\dots,s^{g-1}_{t}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> in group <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The mean <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as a baseline to reduce the variance of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in PPO’s policy update. Indeed, a learned function of the state <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> (where typically <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(s_{t})=V_{\pi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(s_{t})=V_{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>) can be used as a baseline, keeping the policy gradient unbiased. However, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> does not really depend on <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, as it is an average of returns starting from <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This difference <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the bias it introduces is what we analyze in the following Lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Considering an LLM post-training setting, i.e., a deterministic transition function where <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{0:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0:t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a binary reward signal, <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})\leq 1-\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\sum_{a_{k}\neq a^{\text{EOS}}}\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}|s_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EOS</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})\leq 1-\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\sum_{a_{k}\neq a^{\text{EOS}}}\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}|s_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\text{EOS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EOS</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\text{EOS}}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the action generating the end-of-sequence token, and thus terminating the episode.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By definition, the value <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation over the returns from any given state <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\pi}(s_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[G_{0}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{t}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi}(s_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[G_{0}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The sum until <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> can be split into two terms, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0-t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-T</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}V_{\pi}(s_{0})&amp;=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}+\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]]+\gamma^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{k-t}r_{k}\right].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}V_{\pi}(s_{0})&amp;=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}+\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]]+\gamma^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{k-t}r_{k}\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The second term is the expected return from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is nothing but <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\pi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{0})=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]+\gamma^{t}V(s_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{0})=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]+\gamma^{t}V(s_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Delta V(s_{t})&amp;=V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})\\
&amp;\leq V(s_{0})-\gamma^{t}V(s_{t})\\
&amp;\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Delta V(s_{t})&amp;=V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})\\
&amp;\leq V(s_{0})-\gamma^{t}V(s_{t})\\
&amp;\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In our LLM post-training setting, all intermediate rewards are zero, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}=0,\forall t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}=0,\forall t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>. When an EOS-token is selected as action, the reward <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is either 1 (the policy provided the correct answer to the problem) or 0 (the policy provided an incorrect answer). Thus, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{t})\geq 0,\forall s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{t})\geq 0,\forall s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. More interestingly, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> only if there exist cases where the episode ends before timestep <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming every episode is successful, i.e., every EOS-token yields a reward of 1, then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is upper-bounded by the probability of generating at least one EOS-token at any time during an episode. Thus,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]\leq 1-\underbrace{\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\sum_{a_{k}\neq a^{\text{EOS}}}\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}|s_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{probability of not generating}\\
\text{at least one EOS-token in $t$ timesteps}\end{subarray}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mtext>EOS</mtext></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>probability of not generating</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>at least one EOS-token in </mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mtext> timesteps</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\gamma^{k}r_{k}\right]\leq 1-\underbrace{\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\sum_{a_{k}\neq a^{\text{EOS}}}\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}|s_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{probability of not generating}\\
\text{at least one EOS-token in $t$ timesteps}\end{subarray}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Full Version of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 GRPO-𝜆 for rapid reward propagation ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we repurpose the bias-variance trade-off from GAE towards a critic-free policy-update like GRPO.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The policy gradient estimate <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> using traces from generalized advantage estimation <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{GAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">GAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{GAE}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be re-parameterized with a critic-free TD-error <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}A_{\text{GAE}}(s_{t})\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\delta_{t}\sum_{l=0}^{t}(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t-l}|s_{t-l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">GAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}A_{\text{GAE}}(s_{t})\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\delta_{t}\sum_{l=0}^{t}(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t-l}|s_{t-l})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We reorganize the many terms of the policy gradient formula<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
              With the existence of REINFORCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams (1992)</a></cite> and policy gradient methods, several works (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al. (2018)</a></cite>) have used the reformulation of the policy gradients under different settings.</span></span></span> so that the gradient is of the form: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{r_{t}\psi_{t}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{r_{t}\psi_{t}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can depend only on the states, actions, and rewards that occurred before (or immediately after) the arrival of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will approximate for an online estimator of the policy gradient <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{A_{\text{GAE}}(s_{t})\penalty\ \nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>GAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.667em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{A_{\text{GAE}}(s_{t})\penalty\ \nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\penalty\ \sum_{l=0}^{\infty}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\delta_{t+l}^{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\penalty\ \sum_{l=0}^{\infty}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\delta_{t+l}^{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let us introduce the following shorthand:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{t}\coloneqq\nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{t}\coloneqq\nabla_{\theta}\log\penalty\ \pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">then expand the sum:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{0}(\delta_{0}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{1}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{2}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{0}(\delta_{0}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{1}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{2}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\nabla_{1}(\delta_{1}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{2}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{3}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\nabla_{1}(\delta_{1}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{2}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{3}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\nabla_{2}(\delta_{2}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{3}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{4}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\nabla_{2}(\delta_{2}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)\delta_{3}^{V}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\delta_{4}^{V}+\penalty\ \dots)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\penalty\ \dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\penalty\ \dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">group the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> terms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{0}^{V}\nabla_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{0}^{V}\nabla_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\delta_{1}^{V}(\nabla_{1}+(\gamma\lambda)\nabla_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\delta_{1}^{V}(\nabla_{1}+(\gamma\lambda)\nabla_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\delta_{2}^{V}(\nabla_{2}+(\gamma\lambda)\nabla_{1}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\nabla_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\delta_{2}^{V}(\nabla_{2}+(\gamma\lambda)\nabla_{1}+(\gamma\lambda)^{2}\nabla_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\penalty\ ..." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ +\penalty\ ...</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">and summarize:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{t-l}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{t-l}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t-l}\mid s_{t-l})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t-l}\mid s_{t-l})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, by defining eligibility trace as the inner sum in that equation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon_{t}:=\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{t-l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon_{t}:=\sum_{l=0}^{t}{(\gamma\lambda)^{l}\nabla_{t-l}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">and converting to a recursive formula:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\nabla_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\nabla_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=(\gamma\lambda)\epsilon_{t-1}+\nabla_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=(\gamma\lambda)\epsilon_{t-1}+\nabla_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">we have our online generalized advantage estimator for the policy gradient:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\epsilon_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}{\delta_{t}^{V}\epsilon_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">So at each time-step, we compute the gradient term <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{t}=\delta_{t}^{V}\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{t}=\delta_{t}^{V}\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the product of the TD error. The role of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is unchanged, remaining a bias-variance trade-off. For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the problem reduces to the (unbiased) TD(0) function. As we increase <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> towards 1, we reduce the variance of our estimator but increase the bias.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Relation with GRPO’s normalized advantage estimation (NAE)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we consider <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}^{V}=A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>NAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}^{V}=A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The advantage is often used in policy-gradient methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mnih et al. (2016)</a></cite>, where subtracting the value-estimate of the current state is used as a variance-reduction technique:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}^{V}=G_{t}-V(s_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}^{V}=G_{t}-V(s_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>NAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> subtracts <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})\equiv V(s_{0})-V(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> introduced in <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 Bounding the normalized advantage estimation bias ‣ 3 GRPO-𝜆 for rapid reward propagation ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma 1</span></a> results in:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}^{V}=G_{t}-V(s_{0})+\Delta V(s_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}^{V}=G_{t}-V(s_{0})+\Delta V(s_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We can thus potentially reduce the bias from using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by including knowledge about <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In preliminary experiments, we simply added the upper bound for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>NAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{NAE}}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">However, results were inconclusive. The bias bound assumes that the policy is optimal, resulting in the highest potential value for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V</annotation></semantics></math>. GRPO removes this term, resulting in a pessimistic advantage value (compared to having an actual critic). By naively adding the upper bound of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V</annotation></semantics></math>, we surmise this might be over-correcting the bias term, resulting in an optimistic advantage value. This means that including the bound could reinforce action-probabilities that lead to 0-rewards (encouraging false positives) while, in the case of GRPO, it instead reduces action-probabilities that lead to 1-rewards (penalizing the false negatives). In the former case, we are stuck in suboptimal behavior, while in the latter, there could be alternative paths towards solving the problem. As such, a more careful bias correction term is needed. It is important to mention that this only focuses on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> in the GRPO setup, not <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> . Adding eligibility traces balances the bias-variance trade-off, which is one of the reasons why <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> outperforms GRPO. We aim to further this direction in future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Pseudocode</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S3" title="3 GRPO-𝜆 for rapid reward propagation ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section 3</span></a>, we introduce <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> , the variant <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-trace follows the traditional RL literature and applies the trace before the PPO clipping objective. <a href="#algorithm1" title="1 ‣ A.3 Pseudocode ‣ Appendix A GRPO-𝜆 Theory ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">algorithm 1</span></a> (left) represents <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> , with the traces derived from <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 GRPO-𝜆 for rapid reward propagation ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 1</span></a>. Likewise, the trace-inspired <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-weight variant is illustrated in <a href="#algorithm2" title="2 ‣ A.3 Pseudocode ‣ Appendix A GRPO-𝜆 Theory ‣ GRPO-𝜆 : Credit Assignment improves LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">algorithm 2</span></a>. We color code the pseudocodes where <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span> denotes the modifications on the GRPO algorithm done for the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-trace variant of the <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">GRPO-<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span> and <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">red</span> denote the modifications for the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-weight variant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A less rigorous explanation of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-weight variant is that the loss at each step (token) essentially gets reweighted implicitly with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-trace. <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-weight does this reweighting of the loss explicitly. To that, this uses the PPO-clip to provide the td-error, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying the trace weights with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> provides the traces, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{w}_{x_{r}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>w</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{w}_{x_{r}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which then multiplied with the advantage estimated explicitly weighs the loss of different tokens (<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{w}_{x^{i}_{r}}A^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}\log{\pi_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{w}_{x^{i}_{r}}A^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}\log{\pi_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>). However, we observe multiplying that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi^{\theta}_{x_{r}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> results in instability. We alleviate that by soft clamping <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi^{\theta}_{x^{r}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi^{\theta}_{x^{r}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\sigma(\log\pi_{x_{r}^{i}}^{\theta}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\sigma(\log\pi_{x_{r}^{i}}^{\theta}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The choice of the clamping function, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sigmoid</span> can be replaced with <span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tanh</span>. The clamping function, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, (a) ensures linear dependence on the gradient and preserve the spirit of the traces, and (b) acts as a regularization to prevent extreme values.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_top ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>GRPO-<math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-trace)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{ref}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{style}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>style</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{style}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>clip</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{NAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>NAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{NAE}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</div>
